FAITHFUL-PARITY NOTE (real branches only — no fabricated chrome)
  The web `HistoryListRow` is a PURE presentational, slot-based primitive. It has NO data source at all
  — not even `useTranslation`; it maps slot nodes + a few structural props to a `GlassPanel` layout. It
  therefore has NO loading / error / stale / offline branch (nothing to load, fail, go stale, or lose
  connectivity to). Inventing such chrome would fabricate states the source does not have and contradict
  the web spec, so this surface reproduces ONLY the source's REAL branches — exactly as the sibling
  presentational primitives BatteryDelta (0077) and TimeMarker (0074) did. The real, slot-/prop-driven
  branches reproduced + tested: checkbox present/absent (tap-isolated), leading present/absent, route /
  metrics / insight present/absent, hover-revealed actions present/absent, activation none / link
  (web href) / action (web onClick), selected on/off, glow cyan/green/purple/none, chevron shown/hidden.
  Tap-isolation is faithful: the checkbox column and the actions overlay sit OUTSIDE the row's tap
  target (web `e.stopPropagation()`); on touch — where there is no hover — the actions stay reachable
  rather than being stranded (an accessibility-respecting superset of the web `group-hover` reveal).

  i18n: the web source carries ZERO user-facing copy (decorative chevron, no aria-label, caller-composed
  slot text) — so there is no web `t()` key to mirror. The native peer adds exactly ONE string the web
  omits — the VoiceOver hint on an interactive (link/button) row, an Apple HIG affordance — keyed in the
  per-surface "HistoryListRow" table and resolved through the P1/S10 facade (no English literal in code).

